WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.928 --> 00:00:13.369
friends came out of the cafeteria.

2
00:00:13.389 --> 00:00:17.931
"I must get to Metro City Electronics," Roxy thought.

3
00:00:17.951 --> 00:00:23.413
"I'm going to the nurse," she said to her friends.

4
00:00:23.433 --> 00:00:26.234
"I, um, don't feel well.

5
00:00:26.774 --> 00:00:27.935
Maybe it was the tacos!"

6
00:00:28.955 --> 00:00:30.076
Roxy hurried down the hall.

7
00:00:31.444 --> 00:00:32.585
"Gee," Mara said.

8
00:00:32.605 --> 00:00:34.746
"I hope Roxy is okay."

9
00:00:34.766 --> 00:00:38.427
"She's probably fine," Terrell said.

10
00:00:42.149 --> 00:00:44.990
Roxy spotted Detective Smith in front of Metro City Electronics.

11
00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:47.011
She also saw trash.

12
00:00:47.811 --> 00:00:49.732
It was all over the sidewalk and street.

13
00:00:51.012 --> 00:00:51.733
Roxy landed.

14
00:00:51.753 --> 00:00:56.635
"Detective, you shouldn't litter!"

15
00:00:57.655 --> 00:00:58.876
Detective Smith frowned.

16
00:00:59.908 --> 00:01:01.709
"Very funny, Rocket Girl.

17
00:01:02.089 --> 00:01:03.789
The trash hasn't been picked up this week.

18
00:01:04.009 --> 00:01:05.190
It's piling up everywhere."

19
00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:07.950
"Why?" Roxy asked.

20
00:01:09.291 --> 00:01:10.411
Detective Smith shrugged.

21
00:01:10.431 --> 00:01:13.592
"The Smart Brothers stopped answering their phones.

22
00:01:13.992 --> 00:01:16.573
So Mayor Bloom hired a new company to pick up the trash.

23
00:01:17.053 --> 00:01:19.194
I guess the new company forgot some streets."

24
00:01:20.374 --> 00:01:23.955
Just then a garbage truck zoomed by.

25
00:01:23.995 --> 00:01:26.276
Trashman's Trash Pickup was written on the side.

26
00:01:27.512 --> 00:01:29.733
"That's the new company," Detective Smith said.

27
00:01:29.753 --> 00:01:32.015
"I'm sure they'll pick up the garbage soon."

28
00:01:34.116 --> 00:01:36.817
Roxy and Detective Smith went into Metro City Electronics.

29
00:01:38.418 --> 00:01:39.639
An employee hurried over.

30
00:01:39.659 --> 00:01:41.560
"I'm glad you're here.

31
00:01:42.020 --> 00:01:44.562
Someone stole a bunch of things from our warehouse."

32
00:01:46.023 --> 00:01:50.965
She led Roxy and the detective past shelves filled with TVs, speakers, and other electronics.

33
00:01:52.826 --> 00:01:55.148
They went through some doors and entered a big warehouse.

34
00:01:56.264 --> 00:01:58.226
Roxy noticed that many shelves were empty.

35
00:01:58.246 --> 00:02:01.629
"The robber broke in through those doors."

36
00:02:02.389 --> 00:02:05.432
The employee pointed to a set of broken doors in the back of the warehouse.

37
00:02:06.493 --> 00:02:07.714
The doors led to an alley.

38
00:02:08.274 --> 00:02:09.555
Trash filled the alley.

39
00:02:10.316 --> 00:02:13.578
A dumpster overflowed with bags, rotting food, and other garbage.

40
00:02:14.399 --> 00:02:15.560
Detective Smith groaned.

41
00:02:17.382 --> 00:02:20.945
"I hope Trashman's Trash Pickup starts picking up garbage soon!"

42
00:02:22.166 --> 00:02:22.886
Roxy nodded.

43
00:02:22.906 --> 00:02:24.808
"I hope so too, Detective.

44
00:02:25.176 --> 00:02:27.338
But right now we need to solve this robbery."

45
00:02:27.678 --> 00:02:28.779
She turned to the employee.

46
00:02:28.799 --> 00:02:31.081
"Did you see the robbers?"

47
00:02:32.462 --> 00:02:33.542
The employee shook her head.

48
00:02:33.562 --> 00:02:35.804
"I was helping a customer.

49
00:02:36.204 --> 00:02:38.606
Then I came back here to look for a TV for him.

50
00:02:39.067 --> 00:02:41.328
I saw the broken doors and empty shelves."

51
00:02:42.569 --> 00:02:45.532
Vroom! A big truck rumbled down the alley.

52
00:02:46.172 --> 00:02:48.814
Wrappers and scraps of newspaper fluttered through the air.

53
00:02:49.675 --> 00:02:51.036
Detective Smith groaned again.

54
00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:53.621
"That was the garbage truck!

55
00:02:53.861 --> 00:02:56.263
Why didn't they stop here and pick up this trash?"

56
00:02:57.904 --> 00:03:00.246
Roxy watched the truck disappear around a corner.

57
00:03:01.607 --> 00:03:02.947
"I don't know, Detective.

58
00:03:03.408 --> 00:03:05.969
But I'm starting to think it's suspicious."

59
00:03:07.070 --> 00:03:08.551
Just then they heard a voice.

60
00:03:08.571 --> 00:03:11.153
"Someone stole my car!"
